That&#x27;s why we have all this LC_* stuff in Linux, which you can configure to your needs:<p><pre><code>  export  LC_MEASUREMENT=&quot;de_DE&quot;
  export  LC_MONETARY=&quot;de_DE&quot; 
  export  LC_PAPER=&quot;de_DE&quot;                             
  export LC_CTYPE=de_DE.UTF-8  
  export LC_MESSAGES=&quot;en_US.UTF-8&quot;        
  export LC_RESPONSE=&quot;en_US.UTF-8&quot;  
  export LC_TIME=en_US.UTF-8
</code></pre>
Mix in your Swedish or Swaheli, maybe even the Vatican State:<p><pre><code>   e.g. de_DE, sw_TZ, it_VA (not guaranteed ;-).</code></pre>
